{"kind":"request","text":"Retain performance evidence somewhere that survives deleting the implementing worktree.\n\nFound while producing the contract-full fan-out verdict under e1ab6474. The adopted contract requires a run to preserve its raw samples, distributions, case order, environment and digests. The digests, environment, case order and head all survive, because they are published in docs/reference/performance.md. The raw samples do not.\n\nperformance/.gitignore excludes evidence/, so the files are written into the worktree that ran them, and AGENTS.md step 6 deletes that worktree after merge. I searched the checkout, every live worktree, /private/tmp, /var/folders and /tmp for evidence.json, samples.jsonl and candidate.bench from the fan-out run and found none of them. The consequence is narrow but real: docs/reference/performance.md tells readers that the medians must not replace the distributions, and the distributions no longer exist to consult.\n\nThis does not invalidate the published verdict, and it must not be repaired by re-running the campaign. All three digests, the 500-sample population, the per-width sample counts and the four windowed width-one medians were independently recomputed from the raw files while they still existed, and that recomputation is recorded in approved report 07ba1052. What is missing is a place for the next run's evidence to live, not a re-measurement of this one.\n\nFiled as a child of promise c5c7aa17 rather than folded into e1ab6474, because it is a change to the lane's retention mechanism and not part of stating the verdict. The verdict page reports the gap as an honest miss and points here.","body":{"branch":"request/perf-evidence-retention","conditions":"1. Establish where a retained performance run lives after its implementing worktree is deleted. Today performance/.gitignore excludes evidence/, so the only copy of evidence.json, samples.jsonl and candidate.bench sits inside the request worktree, and step 6 of AGENTS.md deletes that worktree after merge. The 500-sample fan-out run measured at 7b5026f0 is already gone this way. 2. Decide deliberately between the available shapes rather than defaulting: commit a reduced retained form for runs that a published verdict cites, keep the raw files outside the worktree at a stable location the page can name, or attach the reduced form to the durable record as evidence. Weigh repository size against the page's own rule that medians must not replace the distributions. 3. Whatever is chosen must let a later reader re-derive every number a performance page publishes, including per-width distributions and windowed medians, or the page must stop claiming the distributions are available. Do not silently weaken the rule to fit the mechanism. 4. Do not re-run the fan-out campaign to recover the lost files. Its digests and an independent recomputation of all three, of the 500-sample population and of the four windowed width-one medians are recorded durably in approved report 07ba1052, which is sufficient for the verdict already published. The gap is retention for the future, not re-measurement of the past. 5. Preserve every contract the performance lane already preserves. Publish an exact-head artifact at each changed stable path, obtain independent review, and update docs/reference/performance.md and performance/README.md if the retention story changes what they promise.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}